fact WorkItem(id: "WI-176", description: some(value: "Wire anthill.persistence.{persist, retract, flush, pull} as interpreter builtins. Today rustland/anthill-core/src/eval/builtins.rs registers prelude/Console/Modify and anthill.reflect.KB.execute, but NOT the four persistence operations declared in stdlib/anthill/persistence/ — so they're unreachable from interpreted anthill code. Required: Interpreter gains a Store registry mapping a Value::Entity (the FileStore(...) term, or other concrete store entity) to a Box<dyn Store>. Four register_if_present entries dispatch from the qualified anthill names to Store::persist / Store::retract / Store::flush / BulkStore::pull. Pull returns a List[Term] (the fact heads of every persisted fact). The shim populates the registry before calling main; programs receive the store as an opaque Value::Entity. Acceptance: integration test where an anthill program asserts a WorkItem fact, calls persist + flush, the file on disk contains the fact, a fresh KB calls pull and the fact reappears. Prerequisite for WI-009 — without this the anthill side has no way to write back to disk. Design: see examples/github-todo/docs/anthill-migration.md §5.2."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-05-05T16:52:20Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-176", author: "claude", content: "Landed: persist, retract, flush builtins under qnames anthill.persistence.Store.{persist,retract,flush}. Plus Interpreter::register_store API and Interpreter::store_canonical_key for entity-keyed store dispatch. NOT landed: pull (BulkStore.pull). Pull would need Stream wrapping for List[Term] return; deferred because WI-009 does pull from the Rust shim side at startup, not from interpreted code. Test: anthill-core/tests/persistence_builtins_test.rs (3 tests, all green).", at: "2026-05-05T16:53:02Z")
